From 4b879280ecbf956328e245e7833cebdf8d93459e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charliechen114514 <725610365@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 23:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] configs: evb-rk3588: enable rockusb gadget + boot-mode
 register
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Turn on the mainline rockusb implementation (cmd/rockusb.c +
f_rockusb.c) — the vendor Loader-mode flash protocol — on the OTG port,
and set CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_BOOT_MODE_REG to the vendor rk3588 value
(0xfd588080); the default 0 compiles setup_boot_mode() out entirely,
leaving the FASTBOOT/UMS reboot-mode branches dead code. USB_GADGET
delta is the same five lines generic-rk3588_defconfig carries;
CMD_USB_MASS_STORAGE rides along for the BOOT_UMS branch.

Signed-off-by: Charliechen114514 <725610365@qq.com>
---
 configs/evb-rk3588_defconfig | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/configs/evb-rk3588_defconfig b/configs/evb-rk3588_defconfig
index 3a8dbfcfbef..77a831610e1 100644
--- a/configs/evb-rk3588_defconfig
+++ b/configs/evb-rk3588_defconfig
@@ -6,6 +6,10 @@ CONFIG_DEFAULT_DEVICE_TREE="rockchip/rk3588-evb1-v10"
 CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_RK3588=y
 CONFIG_SPL_SERIAL=y
 CONFIG_TARGET_EVB_RK3588=y
+# Loader-mode register (vendor rk3588_defconfig value): setup_boot_mode() reads
+# it at boot; the kernel's topeet reboot-mode node (pmu0_grf + 0x80) writes it.
+# 0 would compile the whole boot-mode mechanism out.
+CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_BOOT_MODE_REG=0xfd588080
 CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND="load mmc 0:3 ${scriptaddr} /boot/boot.scr; source ${scriptaddr}"
 CONFIG_SYS_LOAD_ADDR=0xc00800
 CONFIG_DEBUG_UART_BASE=0xFEB50000
@@ -26,6 +30,18 @@ CONFIG_CMD_GPIO=y
 CONFIG_CMD_GPT=y
 CONFIG_CMD_MMC=y
 CONFIG_CMD_USB=y
+# rockusb (Loader mode): the vendor flash protocol on the OTG port — mainline
+# implements it fully (cmd/rockusb.c + f_rockusb.c), VID/PID default to
+# 2207:350b on RK3588. Same delta generic-rk3588_defconfig carries. ums rides
+# along (BOOT_UMS case in boot_mode.c pairs with it). FASTBOOT must stay off:
+# USB_GADGET_DOWNLOAD defaults it to y and FASTBOOT_BUF_ADDR then has no
+# default value → syncconfig asks interactively → background builds hang.
+# CONFIG_USB_FUNCTION_FASTBOOT is not set
+CONFIG_USB_GADGET=y
+CONFIG_USB_GADGET_DOWNLOAD=y
+CONFIG_USB_FUNCTION_ROCKUSB=y
+CONFIG_CMD_ROCKUSB=y
+CONFIG_CMD_USB_MASS_STORAGE=y
 # CONFIG_CMD_SETEXPR is not set
 CONFIG_CMD_REGULATOR=y
 # CONFIG_SPL_DOS_PARTITION is not set
-- 
